---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

const lastUpdated = '5 August 2026';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="How steveharrison.dev and Salary Ticker handle your data."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

			<p>
				This policy covers the website at <strong>steveharrison.dev</strong> and the macOS app
				<strong>Salary Ticker</strong>. Both are operated by Steve Harrison, an individual developer
				based in Australia.
			</p>

			<h2>Salary Ticker (the macOS app)</h2>

			<p>
				<strong>Salary Ticker does not collect, transmit, or store any of your personal data.</strong>
			</p>

			<p>
				The app contains no analytics, no crash reporting, no advertising, and no third-party SDKs of
				any kind. It makes no network connections whatsoever, so nothing you enter can leave your Mac.
			</p>

			<p>
				The settings you enter, such as your daily pay figure and your day start and end times, are
				stored locally on your Mac using the standard macOS preferences system
				(<code>UserDefaults</code>, under the identifier <code>com.salaryticker.app</code>). They are
				never uploaded anywhere, and I have no way to see them.
			</p>

			<p>
				Deleting the app removes it from your Mac. To remove its stored preferences as well, run
				<code>defaults delete com.salaryticker.app</code> in Terminal.
			</p>

			<p>
				The app is distributed from this website and is signed and notarised by Apple under Apple
				Developer Team ID <code>8RTPS5KUF8</code>. Apple may log notarisation checks when you first
				launch the app; that is a function of macOS itself and is covered by
				<a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
					Apple's privacy policy</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>This website</h2>

			<h3>Analytics</h3>

			<p>
				This site uses Google Analytics 4 to understand which pages people visit and which links they
				click. This sets cookies in your browser and sends Google information such as your
				approximate location, browser, device type, and the pages you view. I use this only in
				aggregate, to see what is worth writing more of.
			</p>

			<p>
				I never see your name or email address through analytics. If you would rather not be counted,
				you can install the
				<a
					href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a
				>, use your browser's tracking protection, or block the script. Nothing on this site depends
				on analytics working. Google's handling of this data is covered by
				<a
					href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a
				>.
			</p>

			<h3>Newsletter</h3>

			<p>
				If you choose to subscribe to the newsletter, your email address is submitted to and stored by
				<a href="https://buttondown.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Buttondown</a>,
				which sends the emails on my behalf. I use your address only to send you new articles. I do
				not sell it, rent it, or share it with anyone else. Every email includes an unsubscribe link,
				and unsubscribing removes you from the list.
			</p>

			<h3>Hosting and embedded content</h3>

			<p>
				Like most websites, the server hosting this site may keep standard access logs, including IP
				addresses, for security and reliability. Some pages embed content from third parties such as
				YouTube or link to external sites; those providers have their own privacy policies, and this
				policy does not cover them.
			</p>

			<h2>Your rights</h2>

			<p>
				You can ask me what personal information I hold about you, ask me to correct it, and ask me to
				delete it. In practice the only personal information I hold directly is a newsletter email
				address, if you gave me one. Email me and I will action any request. If you are in the EU or
				UK, or anywhere else with equivalent data protection law, the same applies to you.
			</p>

			<p>
				Some of the services above, including Google Analytics and Buttondown, are based overseas, so
				information collected through them may be stored or processed outside Australia.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>

			<p>
				If this policy changes in a way that matters, I will update the date at the top of this page.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>

			<p>
				Questions about any of this? Email
				<a href="mailto:steve@steveharrison.dev">steve@steveharrison.dev</a>, or find me on
				<a
					href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/stevenanthonyharrison/"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a
				>.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	main {
		max-width: 720px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 1em;
	}

	main > h1 {
		font-size: 2em;
		font-weight: 700;
		margin: 1em 0 0.4em;
	}

	.updated {
		color: rgb(var(--grey));
		font-size: 0.9em;
		margin-bottom: 2em;
	}

	main h2 {
		font-size: 1.25em;
		font-weight: 700;
		margin: 2em 0 0.6em;
		border: none;
		padding: 0;
	}

	main h3 {
		font-size: 1.05em;
		font-weight: 600;
		margin: 1.5em 0 0.5em;
	}

	main p {
		margin-bottom: 1em;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	main code {
		font-size: 0.9em;
		background: rgba(var(--grey-light), 0.5);
		padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
		border-radius: 4px;
	}
</style>
